</td>
</tr><tr id="_62b9fc6e-403f-26d5-e03c-a8caafd10aaf" semx-id="_62b9fc6e-403f-26d5-e03c-a8caafd10aaf"><td id="_5ab939de-3f46-eb33-84b7-15019ffc17f2" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_5ab939de-3f46-eb33-84b7-15019ffc17f2"><p id="_f2fc6188-2cca-54ab-b567-20c7f161d924" semx-id="_f2fc6188-2cca-54ab-b567-20c7f161d924">endLifeSpan      DEFAULT (“Current”)</p>
</td>
<td id="_b035bfed-7124-b959-cfa4-db9b1d8346ad" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_b035bfed-7124-b959-cfa4-db9b1d8346ad"><p id="_5ca5d310-2505-7187-7fc2-c5f2a9cf9c56" semx-id="_5ca5d310-2505-7187-7fc2-c5f2a9cf9c56">End date of a specific instance version. This is the complementary attribute to the StartLifespan attribute. However, since the Explicit Text Format is versioned by dataset it is rare that this attribute would contain any value other than the default “current” so it would normally not be expressed</p>
</td>
</tr><tr id="_6c58c7de-7e90-147f-3df9-b4022e96f0c2" semx-id="_6c58c7de-7e90-147f-3df9-b4022e96f0c2"><td id="_0be76a8d-6ed9-b34e-d669-c5a8d0051281" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_0be76a8d-6ed9-b34e-d669-c5a8d0051281"><p id="_ea4d4cf5-0fef-2fa7-71c1-1eb8b0970169" semx-id="_ea4d4cf5-0fef-2fa7-71c1-1eb8b0970169">dateConsidered</p>
</td>
<td id="_fde00a1b-1eb0-a50c-bfeb-910507960920" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_fde00a1b-1eb0-a50c-bfeb-910507960920"><p id="_4a1f137a-4a0f-4ba2-58c3-ee56e8f6720c" semx-id="_4a1f137a-4a0f-4ba2-58c3-ee56e8f6720c">The date at which the official statement or document was considered by the appropriate governing body</p>
</td>
