<clause id="sec-source-block" anchor="sec-source-block" obligation="normative" semx-id="_e883e047-aebb-76d2-8338-ccced719a2e5">
<title id="_a9891abf-6952-3743-2c56-a2ff76c8252c" semx-id="_26ef5a06-3545-0861-1f6a-154ab73980e3">Source Block</title><fmt-title depth="3" id="_a12c2bf2-04f9-832b-2e97-3661e5041de2"><span class="fmt-caption-label">2<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>5<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>6</span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_a9891abf-6952-3743-2c56-a2ff76c8252c">Source Block</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Clause</span> 2<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>5<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>6</fmt-xref-label>
<p id="_ec051705-d861-e017-ddac-56bb0c8ca7ba" semx-id="_ec051705-d861-e017-ddac-56bb0c8ca7ba">All of the information elements in the S-121 model may be sourced.  This is an important capability of the standard. The Source Block carries the information for a source. The source element includes a large number of optional elements that allow a source to be described. Many of these derive from the ISO metadata standards. The “name” of a source is not normally an alternative for the sID because source document names may be long and complex.</p>

<table id="tbl-sourceblock-optional" anchor="tbl-sourceblock-optional" semx-id="_cee37f2b-24b7-3192-709b-9741c04b682c" autonum="2-11">
