<clause id="sec-profile-point-block" anchor="sec-profile-point-block" obligation="normative" semx-id="_1e4638bd-69f9-ea59-da7a-887907a2a918">
<title id="_a6074e92-d06f-ffa0-226a-15467bd4d4d7" semx-id="_ff78d893-9211-7dac-7505-a981e68b8d65">Profile Point Block</title><fmt-title depth="3" id="_fd17b59e-296f-78eb-9b3b-f65d99a46006"><span class="fmt-caption-label">B<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>11<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>2</span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_a6074e92-d06f-ffa0-226a-15467bd4d4d7">Profile Point Block</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Annex</span> B<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>11<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>2</fmt-xref-label>
<p id="_81fb04e0-6d03-ae9e-708a-8275fe4e7fc1" semx-id="_81fb04e0-6d03-ae9e-708a-8275fe4e7fc1">Lists of points provide the geometry for a set of Locations. A list of points is best described in a table as long as the number of attributes expressed is not excessive. If Location by Text is used then individual Point Blocks rather than a table should be used.</p>

<p id="_3b0a4556-3172-07d7-7d5a-6e30bd877325" semx-id="_3b0a4556-3172-07d7-7d5a-6e30bd877325"><strong>Profile Point Block First Record (multiple Point Blocks may exist or a table may be used):</strong></p>

