</td>
<td id="_833c543c-fc06-f020-64f0-7c135683d115" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_833c543c-fc06-f020-64f0-7c135683d115"><p id="_a7990608-632f-c32f-75b3-e03c2c9b25e0" semx-id="_a7990608-632f-c32f-75b3-e03c2c9b25e0">referenceSystem</p>
</td>
<td id="_97fbcde3-a791-1e74-a27c-3a9457c71815" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_97fbcde3-a791-1e74-a27c-3a9457c71815"><p id="_d1a4888f-e3a8-5780-cc51-4f95426e4e84" semx-id="_d1a4888f-e3a8-5780-cc51-4f95426e4e84">Allows a CoordinateReferencingSystem (CRS) to optionally be specified. In many other S-100 based products the CRS is only defined at the metadata level and applies for the whole data set; however, in S-121 it is necessary to detail it right down to the specific instances of geometry since treaty points and lines may come from different sources such as different treaties that may use different CRS</p>
</td>
</tr><tr id="_d09e20e1-f4a1-6c49-46d3-6c0536c08a8d" semx-id="_d09e20e1-f4a1-6c49-46d3-6c0536c08a8d"><td id="_30523754-2a6c-8a76-2c01-51b922322a47" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_30523754-2a6c-8a76-2c01-51b922322a47"><p id="_226a7f43-b004-dfab-aea2-1916a578dff2" semx-id="_226a7f43-b004-dfab-aea2-1916a578dff2">Original Location:</p>
